# nr-tui-repl: the plain REPL crate native/core/crates/mixdog-repl (`mixdog --plain`)
# Files: Cargo.toml, src/{lib,repl,line_editor,stream_sink,turn_output,slash}.rs, tests/{repl_twin,repl_pty}.rs,
# tests/recorders/record-repl.mjs, tests/goldens/repl.json.
# Nothing here could be compiled (no cargo in this task): the lead compiles it with the wave.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml (hot file)

In `[workspace] members`, after `"crates/mixdog-term",` (keep the list sorted the way it is):

    "crates/mixdog-repl",

In `[workspace.dependencies]`, next to the other internal crates (after `mixdog-tui = { path = "crates/mixdog-tui" }`):

    mixdog-repl = { path = "crates/mixdog-repl" }

The crate asks for these features of already-declared workspace dependencies in its own Cargo.toml: `tokio` with
`rt`, `rt-multi-thread`, `sync`, `macros`, `time`. No new external crate: every dependency is a workspace crate or one of
`async-trait`, `serde_json`, `tokio`, all in the lock.

