## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml (hot file)

Run the workspace-hack refresh for the new member (the crate's Cargo.toml already carries the
`mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }` edge).

## 4. What the binary (nr-tui-entry-argv, the `mixdog` entry) applies

* Depend on `mixdog-repl` and, for `--plain`, call `mixdog_repl::run(mixdog_repl::ReplOptions { provider, model, tool_mode, cwd },
  footer)`; it returns the process exit code (0 quit or end of input, 130 Ctrl+C, 1 the core cannot be reached or the terminal
  fails). `tool_mode` is `"full"` (the default, `ReplOptions::default()`) or `"readonly"`.
* `footer` is an `Arc<dyn mixdog_repl::Footer>`: `mixdog_tui::footer::StatuslineRenderer` implements it, so the entry builds the
  one renderer per process the way nr-tui-footer's wire says (host, io, paths, background, clock, style) and passes
  `Arc::new(renderer)`; the REPL renders one line per turn and after `/clear`, from caches the renderer's background job keeps.
* `mixdog_repl::run` calls `mixdog_launch::ensure_core::ensure_core(EnsureOptions::default())` before it connects, as the TUI
  does, and prints `mixdog: <reason>` to stderr when it fails. The process lifecycle ledger (`begin_process_lifecycle` /
  `finish_process_lifecycle`) stays the entry's: it brackets the call.
* The `--help` / `-h` short-circuit of `runRepl` (print the help, exit 0 before any session) is the entry's argv handling.

## 5. Protocol, compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING, rows

No protocol method, no row, no SERVICE_PENDING entry: the REPL is a client of methods the core already serves
(`thread/start`, `turn/start`, `thread/clear`, `thread/compact/start`, `route/set`, the output-style and tool-mode actions of the
session store).

## 6. Core gap the lead should decide (not a wiring step)

`/model <name>` of the Node REPL validated the selector (`setRoute(request, { validateOnly: true })`) BEFORE it compacted the
conversation, so an unknown model failed without touching the chat. `route/set` always writes (`plan()` in
mixdog-core-domains `route_set_service.rs` sets `validate_only: false` and `OPTION_KEYS` has no `validateOnly`), so the REPL
compacts first (when the conversation is established, the model really changes and `onModelChange` is not off) and then
sets the route; an unknown selector is reported by `route/set` after the compaction. Accepting `validateOnly` in the `route/set`
selection (add it to `OPTION_KEYS` and pass it as `SetRouteOptions.validate_only`) lets the REPL restore the order with one
more `setRoute` call before `compact` in `slash.rs` `set_model`.

## 7. Notes for the lead

* Twin: `tests/repl_twin.rs` replays `tests/goldens/repl.json` (34 stream/final-render cases and 62 slash cases, colour on and off).
  The golden was recorded with
  `node tests/recorders/record-repl.mjs --tree D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node --write tests/goldens/repl.json` and is checked with
  `--check` (same command, `--tree C:/Project/mixdog` is the same code).
* `tests/repl_pty.rs` replays the REPL's output on the VT grid of mixdog-term (the in-process terminal); it starts no pty, binary
  or core. `mixdog-testkit/tests/cfg_test_guard.rs` is not affected (mixdog-repl is not one of its LIBRARIES).
